  <name>Brisa</name>
  <name xml:lang="es">Brisa</name>

  <summary>Compiler and manager for native PC ports, based on manifests</summary>
  <summary xml:lang="es">Compilador y gestor de ports nativos de PC, basado en manifiestos</summary>

  <description>
    <p>
      Brisa is a compiler and manager for native PC ports (decompilation
      projects released on GitHub), in the style of EmuDeck and built on
      machine-readable JSON manifests. It scans a single ROM directory, links
      each ROM where the port expects it, installs and updates ports from their
      GitHub releases, and manages per-game mods with symlinks — keeping saves
      and configuration safe across updates.
    </p>
    <p>
      It ships a native desktop interface (gamepad-friendly game mode included)
      and a full CLI, so it also works headless or integrated with Steam via
      generated launchers. All data stays in a single user folder
      (roms/, ports/, mods/...).
    </p>
    <p>Brisa does not include or download ROMs: ports require the original game, of which the user must own a legal copy. All managed software is open source (decompilations).</p>
  </description>

